        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A laser level replaces the single most tedious part of any layout job: transferring a level line across a room without accumulating error. The catch is that laser levels vary enormously in what they actually project, and buying a simple cross-line laser when you needed 360-degree coverage means doing the job three times. Here is how to match the type to the work, and which tools hold their accuracy.
